# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-46600 (GHSA-gg3m-vvp2-p2c5, GO-2026-5942) — golang.org/x/net:
# out-of-bounds read / panic parsing an invalid SVCB or HTTPS DNS RR
#
# Found in: usr/local/bin/yq
# Fixed in: golang.org/x/net 0.56.0
#
# Same situation as the task/yq/cosign entries above: yq is an official
# upstream GitHub release binary, compiled by its own maintainers against
# whatever golang.org/x/net version they'd vendored at release time — not
# something our own version-pinning can reach independently of an
# upstream rebuild. Live-checked 2026-08-15 by inspecting go.mod directly
# at mikefarah/yq's latest available tag (v4.53.3, identical to what we
# already install): it declares `golang.org/x/net v0.55.0`, one minor
# release short of the 0.56.0 fix. No newer yq release exists as of this
# date. The affected symbols are in golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage
# (DNS SVCB/HTTPS record parsing) — yq itself has no DNS-resolution code
# path that would invoke them, so this is a dependency-presence finding
# rather than a reachable one, but it is left in .trivyignore rather than
# silently dropped: Trivy's SCA scan is version-based, not reachability-
# based, and will keep flagging it regardless of actual exploitability
# until yq ships against a newer golang.org/x/net.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-11-10

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools: path traversal in PackageIndex
#
# Found in: pip's own vendored copy (pip/_vendor/setuptools), NOT the
# top-level `setuptools` distribution — a `pip install --upgrade
# setuptools` in the Dockerfile does not reach this at all, since it's
# bundled source inside pip's own package rather than a package pip's own
# dependency resolver manages for itself.
#
# Fixed in: setuptools 78.1.1. Live-checked 2026-08-15 against pip's own
# vendor.txt across every release from 25.0 through the current latest
# (26.2.1) and the main branch: all of them vendor exactly 70.3.0. This
# is not something any pip upgrade in our own Dockerfile can fix — it
# requires pip's own upstream maintainers to bump their vendored copy,
# which has not happened in any release yet. Same category as the
# task/yq/cosign Go-stdlib entries above: a dependency frozen inside a
# third-party redistributed artifact, confirmed unfixable from our side
# against the actual current upstream source, not assumed.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-10

# ==============================================================================
# 2026-08-15 batch — Go 1.26.6 / 1.25.13 stdlib CVEs
#
# DIFFERENT SITUATION from every entry above, and deliberately given a
# SHORTER exp: instead of the standing 2026-11-10 checkpoint. Every entry
# above is "stuck" — investigated and confirmed there is genuinely nothing
# to upgrade to, for months at a stretch (pip's own vendored setuptools
# hasn't moved across dozens of pip releases; Moby's docker.io dependency
# is architecturally stuck until Docker's own plugins move off v28). This
# batch is the opposite: Go 1.26.6 and 1.25.13, released 2026-08-13 (two
# days before this investigation), fixed all nine CVEs below in the
# standard library itself. The fix EXISTS. What doesn't exist yet is a new
# release of any of the tools below built against the patched toolchain —
# live-checked every one's actual latest release against that 2026-08-13
# date:
#
# task v3.52.0 released 2026-07-02 (yq v4.53.3 released 2026-06-06)
# gh v2.97.0 released 2026-07-31 (cosign v3.1.3 released 2026-08-06)
# buildx v0.36.1 released 2026-08-04 (compose v5.4.0 released 2026-08-03)
# docker/cli latest tag v29.7.2 (via git ls-remote; no release predates the patch either)
#
# Every single one predates 2026-08-13 — none of them COULD contain the
# fix yet, this is not a gap in our own checking.
#
# EXPIRY UPDATED 2026-08-27, exp:2026-08-29 -> exp:2026-09-05: this was a
# DATE ALIGNMENT with the separately-added CVE-2026-17106 (buildx)
# checkpoint below, to consolidate two review passes into one — it is NOT
# a re-verification that these nine still lack fixes. Nothing above was
# re-checked as part of this change. Whoever does the Sept 5 review owes
# this batch the same live-release check described above, not just the
# buildx one: re-run this scan, and drop whichever of these nine have
# since been picked up by a fresh task/yq/gh/cosign/buildx/compose/
# docker-cli release (config/resolve.sh's own "latest" tracking should
# pull those in automatically on the next lockfile update, no Dockerfile
# change needed for that part). If any are still unfixed on Sept 5,
# re-verify and extend deliberately — don't let a second silent push-
# forward happen.
#
# Found in: usr/bin/docker, usr/libexec/docker/cli-plugins/docker-buildx,
# usr/libexec/docker/cli-plugins/docker-compose, usr/local/bin/cosign,
# usr/local/bin/gh, usr/local/bin/task, usr/local/bin/yq
#
# (usr/bin/pebble also carried these same findings — that one is handled
# by removing the unused binary outright in the Dockerfile instead of an
# ignore entry, since nothing in this image actually runs it.)
#
# ADDED 2026-08-27: CVE-2026-56864 and CVE-2026-56865 belong to this same
# Go 1.26.6/1.25.13 security release (golang.org/x/mod transparency-log
# tile-verification bypass) but were missed in the 2026-08-15 pass — a
# live Trivy scan two days before this batch's own exp: date surfaced
# them as active, unignored failures in gh, cosign, docker-buildx, and
# docker-compose. Same root cause, same affected-binary subset, same
# "fix exists upstream, no tagged release incorporates it yet" situation
# as the seven original entries above — confirmed specifically for gh (cli/cli's own repo
# has merged "Bump Go to 1.26.6" but v2.98.0, current latest, predates
# that merge per its own changelog). Given how close this already is to
# the batch's exp: date, do not extend blindly on 2026-08-29 without
# re-checking each of the nine CVEs in this batch individually — some may
# have shipped fixes by then and some may not.
# ==============================================================================
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-09-05
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-09-05
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-09-05
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-09-05
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-09-05
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-09-05
